SEG = "PER"
CAT = "fvicPermits"
Q = [
    ("Before acquiring any category A or B longarm in Victoria, a licence holder needs:",
     "A permit to acquire", ["A club endorsement", "A dealer's quote", "A storage certificate"],
     "Section 102(1) makes it an offence to acquire a category A or B longarm without a permit to acquire that firearm. A permit is needed for every category."),
    ("Once issued, a Victorian permit to acquire stays in force for at most:",
     "28 days", ["7 days", "90 days", "12 months"],
     "Section 110 says a permit to acquire continues in force for 28 days, or until the firearm is acquired or the permit is cancelled, whichever comes first."),
    ("When does the 28-day wait in s 107 apply to a permit to acquire?",
     "If you own no registered firearm", ["For every permit you apply for", "Only for category C or D firearms", "Only for second-hand firearms"],
     "Section 107(1) applies the 28-day wait to an applicant who does not possess a registered firearm under a licence. For others, the permit waits only as long as needed to consider it properly."),
    ("A permit to acquire application must state:",
     "The usual storage address", ["The seller's home address", "The price being paid", "The club you shoot at"],
     "Section 106(1A) requires the application to specify the address where the firearm will ordinarily be stored."),
    ("For a permit to acquire a category B longarm, the Chief Commissioner considers whether your need could be met by:",
     "A category A longarm", ["A borrowed category B rifle", "A club-owned centre fire rifle", "An airgun or air rifle"],
     "Section 104(2)(a) requires regard to whether the need cannot be satisfied by a category A longarm, and s 104(2)(b) to the firearms you already possess."),
    ("A category D licence holder already owns a semi-automatic rifle. A permit for a second semi-automatic rifle will:",
     "Not be issued", ["Be issued after 28 days", "Be issued with a club letter", "Need a dealer's consent"],
     "Section 104(1)(d)(iii)(A) bars a permit for a semi-automatic rifle in category C or D if the applicant already possesses another semi-automatic rifle."),
    ("You agree to buy a rifle from a neighbour who is not a dealer. Under s 95 you must:",
     "Engage a dealer as your agent", ["Meet at a police station", "Sign a written private contract", "Pay by bank transfer only"],
     "Section 95 says a person who is not a dealer must not acquire a longarm from another non-dealer unless a licensed firearms dealer is engaged as agent in the transaction."),
    ("Selling your shotgun privately to a licensed friend, s 96 says the sale must go through:",
     "A licensed firearms dealer", ["The Game Management Authority", "Your shooting club secretary", "A justice of the peace"],
     "Section 96 bars a non-dealer from disposing of a firearm to another non-dealer unless a licensed firearms dealer acts as agent."),
    ("Under s 98, a person who is not a dealer may take possession of a firearm only by:",
     "Receiving it personally", ["Having it posted", "Using a courier", "Collecting it from a locker"],
     "Section 98(1) says a non-dealer must not take possession of a firearm by any means other than personally receiving possession of it."),
    ("You move to Victoria from Queensland with your rifle. You must notify the Chief Commissioner within:",
     "7 days of arriving", ["24 hours of arriving", "28 days of arriving", "3 months of arriving"],
     "Section 115 requires notice in the approved form within 7 days after bringing a firearm into the State to keep it here."),
    ("You are moving interstate and taking your firearms. Under s 116, notice of removal must be given:",
     "At least 7 days before", ["Within 7 days after", "Within 14 days after", "On the day you leave"],
     "Section 116(2)(b) requires notice not less than 7 days before the firearm is removed from the State."),
    ("Immediately after registering a firearm, the Chief Commissioner issues the person who possesses it:",
     "A registration certificate", ["A permit to carry it", "A storage approval notice", "A new licence card"],
     "Section 117 requires a certificate of registration setting out the registration details and the possessor's name."),
    ("A police officer asks you to produce your registered rifle for inspection. Under s 120 you:",
     "Must produce it", ["May refuse without a warrant", "Need only show the licence", "Must first ask your club"],
     "Section 120(1) requires the person in whose name a firearm is registered to produce it for inspection at any place when a police officer requests it."),
    ("The Chief Commissioner tells you in writing to have a serial number stamped on your firearm. You must comply within:",
     "28 days", ["7 days", "14 days", "6 months"],
     "Section 119A(2) requires compliance within 28 days of the notice, unless within that time you apply under s 119B to use another method."),
    ("Under s 134C, possessing a firearm whose serial number has been filed off is:",
     "Unlawful without an excuse", ["Lawful if it is registered", "Lawful for any collector", "Lawful on a farm only"],
     "Section 134C makes it an offence to possess, without reasonable excuse, a firearm with no serial number, and s 134C(4) says an erased number counts as no number."),
    ("A category A licence holder wants to buy centre fire cartridges for a friend's rifle. Under s 124(2), this is:",
     "Not allowed", ["Allowed with a receipt", "Allowed at a range", "Allowed in small amounts"],
     "Section 124(2) bars a licence holder from possessing ammunition not suitable for the category of firearms the licence covers. Centre fire rifles are category B."),
    ("Before a shop sells you cartridge ammunition, s 125 says you must produce:",
     "A licence that covers it", ["A Medicare card", "A permit to acquire", "A storage receipt"],
     "Section 125 bars disposing of ammunition to a person who does not produce a licence to possess a firearm that the ammunition suits, or other listed evidence."),
    ("A licensed adult wants to give a 16-year-old nephew a .22 rifle as a birthday present. Under s 136 this:",
     "Is not allowed", ["Is fine with consent", "Is fine for juniors", "Is fine if registered"],
     "Section 136 makes it an offence to dispose of a firearm to a person under 18. A junior licence holder carries or uses a licensed adult's firearm under supervision instead."),
    ("You notice a buyer has been drinking heavily. Under s 133, you must not:",
     "Sell or give them a firearm", ["Talk to them about firearms", "Show them your licence", "Ask them to come back later"],
     "Section 133 makes it an offence to dispose of a firearm to a person you reasonably believe to be under the influence of intoxicating liquor or a drug."),
    ("According to the Firearm Safety Code booklet, where can you hand in an unwanted firearm?",
     "To police or a dealer", ["To any shooting club", "To a council tip", "To a gunsmith only"],
     "The booklet says unwanted firearms and ammunition can be handed to Victoria Police, including a Divisional Firearms Officer, or to a licensed firearms dealer."),
    ("Under s 135, owning a category A rifle that you are not licensed to possess is:",
     "Against the law", ["Lawful if a friend stores it", "Lawful for 90 days", "Lawful if it is unregistered"],
     "Section 135(1) makes it an offence to own a category A or B longarm unless a licence under the Act authorises you to possess it."),
    ("An executor finds firearms in a deceased estate. The Firearm Safety Code booklet says ownership transfer or disposal should be managed within:",
     "6 months of the death", ["28 days of the death", "2 years of the death", "5 years of the death"],
     "The booklet says executors need to prioritise and manage the transfer of ownership or safe disposal of firearms in the estate within 6 months of the owner's death."),
    ("A dealer helping with a private sale as your agent may charge you:",
     "Up to the prescribed amount", ["Whatever the market allows", "A share of the sale price", "Any fee your club sets"],
     "Section 97 says a licensed firearms dealer must not charge more than the prescribed amount for acting as an agent under s 95 or s 96."),
    ("A South Australian with an interstate permit to acquire buys a rifle in Victoria. The permit must have been issued no more than:",
     "28 days before", ["7 days before", "90 days before", "6 months before"],
     "Section 102(5) exempts an interstate permit holder from needing a Victorian permit if the interstate permit was issued not more than 28 days before and the buyer attends the dealer's premises in person."),
]
